## 1.The Narrative

You are between 19-24 and want to make an impact on the future and the world around you. **Standing on the edge of adulthood, you do not know exactly what lies ahead.** You may be wondering if college is next. Potentially you’ve already started higher education, pursued a trade, taken a year off school, started a job that isn’t interesting to you anymore or simply feel stuck in a rut. **Up until now, the last 18 years of your life have been mostly learning**. And most of that time has likely been spent in a classroom setting.
{% /gridSquare %}

{% gridSquare
   contentType="color"
   backgroundColor="#3d2e1f"
   textColor="light"
   aspectRatio="square"
   width="auto"
   height="auto" %}
## 2.The Question

After the majority of your education has been spent in a classroom setting, we are generally given a few options for the future. Most of these options include more classroom settings without gaining hands-on experience, or you hear the infamous line **“welcome to the real world, kid”** as you enter the workforce. What if there’s another option? **What if this isn’t real “life”? What if Jesus intends much more for us as we enter these next formative years?**&nbsp;
{% /gridSquare %}
{% /squareGrid %}

{% ctaSection
   heading="3.The Solution"
   description="BOLD is the solution to the learning method gap and your next step into adulthood. The program has been designed to continue the learning process while putting the last 18 years of classroom experience and growth into real-life practice. We have created a space where young adults can explore the workforce in line with their personal interests. We provide them with affordable housing (free for 2026-2027), personalized financial guidance, biblical community, independence, the ability to decide if college or career are their next step, and a place to set personal growth goals. The narrative has shifted because of the BOLD program. You are now able to launch into the adventure of adulthood with other Christians while doing life together in a safe and vibrant community that is focused on becoming disciples of Jesus."
   variant="brown"
   external=false /%}

{% ctaSection
   heading="Program Overview"
   description="BOLD is a gap year program for graduated high school seniors, current students and recent college graduates (or age 19-24). It is aimed at equipping individuals to become more like Christ while immersing them into “real life” experiences as they better discover who they are as a young adult and pursue future career paths. Examples of ways in which participants will impact the world around them include balancing an off-site job, attending a local church, serving at camp, setting a personal budget, and reaching goals that shape them more into the image of our Creator. A primary goal of this program is to equip, guide, and build confident young men and women to serve as leaders during our Summer Camps between June and July. Through authentic Christian community, hands-on skill development, service, and adventure, participants will prepare to enter the next phase of life grounded in faith, ready to guide the future generations into a transformative way of living."
   buttonLabel="Learn More"
